// TF_DS_FUSED_ROPE_STORE (0198, off by default).
//
// WARP ALIGNMENT (load-bearing, see rope_store.warpShapesOk + its tests): every full-mask warp primitive below
// (`__shfl_xor_sync(0xffffffffu, ...)` in tf_ds_latent_element and tf_ds_fp4_amax, and the key/query amax's
// `__reduce_max_sync` over the whole warp) requires its participating lanes to be one whole warp of consecutive
// element indices.
// An inactive lane inside such a shuffle is undefined behaviour, not a wrong number. It holds only because
//   * D % 64 == 0: D/2 (the latent's packed half row) is warp-aligned, so element i's rotary partner is the neighbour
//     lane's, and the key's 32-element _fp4_store scale groups are a warp;
//   * RD is even: the rotary suffix starts at D - RD, an even column, so the xor-1 pair is (even, odd) inside a warp;
//   * blockDim.x is a multiple of 32 and every stride steps in whole warps (`i += blockDim.x`,
//     `blockDim.x * threadIdx.y`), so a loop's tail leaves whole warps idle rather than single lanes.
// A refactor that flattens indexing, folds rotation into packing, or changes a block shape must keep all three; the
